            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "In addition to spatially varying SAM-temperature rela- tionships, other factors contribute to the differences in climate signals of East and West Antarctica. The West Antarctic and South Pacific sector is strongly influenced by atmospheric circulation anomalies originating as Rossby wave-trains forced from deep convection anomalies over the tropical Pacific on intraseasonal, interannual (ENSO)",
